# Damayan Match — Full Revamp Implementation Plan

A complete overhaul of the existing Damayan app to align with the **final Damayan Match specification**: a barangay-centered relief goods matching system for disaster response.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **This is a major architectural overhaul.** The existing app has features (Admin dashboard, volunteer hub, financial ledger, map view, SMS gateway, multi-center management) that are **explicitly out of scope** in the new specification. These will be removed and replaced with the focused Damayan Match feature set.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking changes**: All existing user data in localStorage will be invalidated. The store schema changes fundamentally. The routing structure changes. Users will need to re-register after the revamp.

> [!CAUTION]
> **The app is client-side only (no backend).** All data is simulated in Zustand + localStorage. The 24-hour timer, QR codes, and verification flows are all simulated. This is a **prototype/demo**, not a production system.

---

## Open Questions

1. **Aesthetic direction**: The current app uses the "Organic Tech" preset (Moss/Clay/Cream palette with Plus Jakarta Sans + Cormorant Garamond). Should we keep this aesthetic or shift to something different for the revamp? I recommend **keeping the current palette** since it fits the community/disaster-response feel well, but will refresh the overall design language.

2. **QR Code generation**: Should we use a library like `qrcode.react` to generate actual scannable QR codes for the verification system, or use a simulated visual placeholder?

3. **Landing page**: The current landing page is a full cinematic hero section with animated feature cards. Should we keep this as a marketing/informational page, or replace it with a simpler entry point that routes directly to login/register?

